;; VERIFIED DIVERGENCE — a top-level define that shadows a builtin is ignored
;; by the VM when that builtin is lowered to a dedicated opcode.
;;
;; R7RS 5.3.1 makes a top-level identifier redefinable, and there is nothing
;; special about a name the implementation happens to use for a builtin: a
;; user's top-level (define (car x) ...) is a definition of `car`, and every
;; subsequent reference must resolve to it.
;;
;; Native honours this. The parser maps some builtin names to dedicated OP tags
;; for a direct C-runtime call, which used to swallow user definitions of those
;; names; codegen now checks user scope first and routes the call through
;; codegenCall when the user has a same-named define (audit Bug G, see
;; userShadowableOps / hasUserShadow in lib/backend/llvm_codegen.cpp). So on
;; native both lines below print the user's answer.
;;
;; The VM's compiler has the same premature-binding decision and no equivalent
;; check: compile_form()'s dispatch chain recognises `car` by spelling and emits
;; the OP_CAR opcode before local resolution ever runs, so the user's define is
;; never consulted. Names the VM resolves by lookup instead of by opcode --
;; `length` here -- do honour the shadow, which is why this is a partial
;; divergence rather than a missing feature.
;;
;; EXPECTED (native, and what R7RS requires):
;;   111
;;   222
;; ACTUAL (VM):
;;   9      <- builtin car ran; the user's definition was dropped
;;   222
;;
;; Fixing it means giving the VM compiler the same user-scope check native has:
;; the head symbol of a call must be looked up in the user's top-level defines
;; before the opcode dispatch chain claims it. That is a change to the whole
;; dispatch chain rather than to one form, and it needs its own differential
;; run over the corpus, so it is filed rather than folded into the R7RS 5.3.1
;; redefinition fix -- which is about *which* definition of a name wins, and is
;; verified on both substrates by corpus/36_toplevel_redefinition.esk.

(define (car x) 111)
(define (length x) 222)

(display (car (list 9 8 7)))
(newline)
(display (length (list 9 8 7)))
(newline)
